### Estate CRM Auth API — Manual HTTP Tests
### Run with: VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP Client, or httpie
### Prerequisites: server running on localhost:3000, database seeded

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Login as admin
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "admin123!"
}

### 2. Get current user (copy access_token cookie from login response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Cookie: access_token=PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Login as agent
# @name agentLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent1@test.com",
  "password": "agent123!"
}

### 4. Login with wrong password (should 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword!"
}

### 5. Login with missing fields (should 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

### 6. Login with short password (should 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "short"
}

### 7. Get /me without cookie (should 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 8. Logout (copy cookie from login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Cookie: access_token=PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 9. Swagger docs
GET http://localhost:3000/api/docs
